Citation rule (machine-enforced): cite existing code with
`path/to/file.ext:line` ONLY after reading that location — a
deterministic checker verifies every line-anchored citation against
the workspace and force-revises the design on any miss. For code you
PROPOSE to add, never attach line numbers.

## Task

Draft the feature design markdown. When installed skills are
present, plan the design so build and test verbs flow through
those skills' documented conventions (read the SKILL.md at the
listed paths for the exact command surface). Treat the fallback
commands as a secondary path used only when no matching skill
exists.

If `revise_reason` is non-empty, this is a revision pass — read
the reason and revise the design accordingly.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task design-author
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task design-author \
    --set design='<design markdown>' \
    --set 'decisions[].decision=<decision>' \
    --set 'decisions[-1].rationale=<why>' \
    --set 'open_risks[]=<risk>'
```
